# ICN Jobs Literature Review — Index

Master catalog of all wiki pages and their relationships. Populated automatically after ingest.

## Studies

Key research studies and reports:

| Page | First Observed | Last Updated | Description |
|------|---------------|-------------|-------------|
| [[ferdman-2026-ai-deskilling-structural-problem]] | 2026-07-10 | 2026-09-25 | Avigail Ferdman's 2026 paper in AI & Society presenting a structural analysis of how AI systems can undermine human capacities through systemic environmental conditions rather than individual failings. Introduces the critical distinction between capacity-hostile and capacity-conducive environments, analyzes the role of agential control and habituation in capacity development, and examines how Artificial Personal Assistants may create capacity-hostile environments by encouraging plan-following rather than plan-forming. The paper argues that deskilling should be understood as a structural problem requiring societal solutions rather than merely an individual responsibility issue. Expanded with detailed analysis of methodology, key findings, market research implications, specific examples, and evaluation frameworks for AI tools. |

## Concepts

Cross-cutting ideas, trends, and theoretical frameworks:

| Page | First Observed | Last Updated | Description |
|------|---------------|-------------|-------------|
| [[capacity-hostile-environments]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Socio-technical contexts that restrict or narrow the field of affordances for human capacity development. Encourages shallow skilling and disrupts habituation. |
| [[capacity-conducive-environments]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Environments that actively afford opportunities for cultivating core human capacities and encourage the capacity to will without demanding virtuous superheroes. |
| [[developmental-perfectionism]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Neo-Aristotelian framework understanding flourishing as a unified life achieved through competent exercise of core human capacities (epistemic, social, moral, creative, volitional). |
| [[agential-control]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | The ability to adjust action execution as it unfolds; distinguishes skills from habits. Loss of agential control is a primary mechanism of capacity-deskilling. |
| [[habituation]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Gradual process of skill acquisition requiring practice, intersubjectivity (mentorship, shared valuing), and embodiment (participatory sense-making). |
| [[affordances]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Action possibilities formed by agent-environment relationship. Invitations to act that are constitutive of flourishing. |
| [[affordance-shrinkage]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Systematic, enduring reduction in action possibilities that discourages compensation for deskilling, often caused by AI automation. |

## Skills

Skills, competencies, and requirements:

| Page | First Observed | Last Updated | Description |
|------|---------------|-------------|-------------|
| [[critical-thinking]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Core epistemic capacity involving theoretical/practical rationality. Eroded by AI overreliance; requires agential control and habituation. |
| [[practical-wisdom]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Phronesis; doing the right thing for the right reason. Requires real-world experience and is undermined by constant APA reliance. |
| [[plan-forming]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Self-constituting activity of settling and coordinating intentions. Requires epistemic, social, moral, creative, and volitional capacities. |
| [[plan-following]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Habit-like response to AI outputs. Lacks agential control, shifts responsibility to AI, undermines self-growth and practical wisdom. |

## Roles

Job roles, positions, and career paths:

| Page | First Observed | Last Updated | Description |
|------|---------------|-------------|-------------|
| [[mentor]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | Guides novice to expert. Instills know-how and shared valuing. Essential for intersubjective habituation and moral development. |
| [[artificial-personal-assistant]] | 2026-09-25 | 2026-09-25 | LLM application that adapts to user needs. Risks creating capacity-hostile environments by encouraging plan-following and offloading life-planning. |

